# What static heuristics found

A deterministic scan already ran over the same source. Each hit is evidence to confirm or reject, not a verdict:
confirm it when you can see what it points at and it is a default, reject it when the scan misread the code or
the choice is deliberate, and add what it could not see, such as copy that restates the heading or a nested
radius that does not line up.

