# Your answer

Answer with one JSON object:

- `summary`: one line, the verdict a designer would give out loud.
- `findings`: one per indicator you judge present, ordered by impact. Each has `indicator` (the catalog name,
  exactly), `layer`, `location` (element, selector, line, or region of the image), `evidence` (quote the text or
  CSS value, or describe what you see), `deliberate`, `rationale` (one or two sentences), and `impact`
  (`high`, `medium` or `low`: how much removing it would improve the design). Do not report an indicator you
  cannot point at.
- `score`: the number of distinct indicators present as defaults, deliberate ones excluded, from 0 to 20.
- `fixes_first`: the three fix names to make first, from the fixes catalog, cheapest high-impact subtraction
  first. Fewer when fewer apply.
